    "created_at": "2026-02-04T10:37:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-04T10:45:48Z",
    "body": "Not WPT ready, but all browsers appear to run both queued javascript URL navigations:\n\n```html\n<script>\nwindow.onload = () => {\n    const anchor = document.createElement(\"a\");\n    document.body.appendChild(anchor);\n\n    anchor.href = \"javascript:globalThis.first = true; console.log('Executed script 1');\";\n    anchor.click();\n\n    anchor.href = \"javascript:globalThis.second = true; console.log('Executed script 2');\";\n    anchor.click();\n\n    setTimeout(() => {\n      console.log(`first ${globalThis.first} second ${globalThis.second}`);\n      anchor.remove();\n    }, 500);\n}\n</script>\n```\nAnd don't cancel the ongoing javascript navigation for anchor.\n\nLadybird only runs the second after https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/976d272c722f9714461afcb4b299f2ab03a50c7a",
